data/works/ — a history-database writing's own words (docs/history/499), written by tools/works-text.py.

WR-0001 First Clement
  Greek:   Kirsopp Lake's Greek text, The Apostolic Fathers I (Loeb, 1912). The text is public domain (Lake died 1946).
           Transcription: First1KGreek, Open Greek and Latin, tlg1271.tlg001.1st1K-grc1, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
           (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Apparatus notes left out; otherwise as transcribed.
           This file's Greek is shared under the same licence, with this credit.
           https://github.com/OpenGreekAndLatin/First1KGreek
  English: J. B. Lightfoot's translation, The Apostolic Fathers (1891). Public domain (Lightfoot died 1889).
           Text as printed by the Christian Classics Ethereal Library, https://www.ccel.org/ccel/lightfoot/fathers.ii.i.html

WR-0002 Letter of Aristeas (docs/history/504), one card a numbered section (1-322), written by tools/aristeas-text.py.
  English: H. T. Andrews' translation, in R. H. Charles (ed.), The Apocrypha and Pseudepigrapha of the Old Testament in English,
           2 vols (Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1913), II. Public domain (Andrews died 1928). Text as CCEL prints it,
           http://www.ccel.org/c/charles/otpseudepig/aristeas.htm
  Left out: Thackeray's English (1904) and any Greek text — the only reachable copies are unproofed OCR scans whose section
           numbers are lost or garbled, and the owner said "no taking risks".
